{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And He spoke.</b> By the way of truth it is not fitting for the discerning to question the deeds of HaShem, why He did so, for all His deeds are in wisdom, and human wisdom is as nothing compared to Him. And I have mentioned this because you will see in this passage that HaShem commanded that they turn back by way of stealth, so that Pharaoh would go out and pursue after them, and drown in the sea, and the thoughts of HaShem are deep:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:15.747172294Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}